<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
      In that loud world, Noah kept a different rhythm.<break time="500ms"/>
      Genesis says he walked with God.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Not as a performance, but as a steady companionship.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Picture Noah in ordinary days.<break time="500ms"/>
      Waking to the morning air.<break time="500ms"/>
      Doing the work that needed doing.<break time="500ms"/>
      Speaking with his family.<break time="500ms"/>
      And returning, again and again, to the quiet presence of God.<break time="1800ms"/>

      When God spoke to Noah, it was not chaos.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was clear instruction.<break time="500ms"/>
      A warning, and also a rescue.<break time="1000ms"/>

      Noah received it without rushing ahead.<break time="500ms"/>
      He began with what was in front of him.<break time="500ms"/>
      The next faithful step.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Maybe he walked the land and chose where the ark would stand.<break time="500ms"/>
      Maybe he counted days and gathered tools.<break time="500ms"/>
      Maybe he explained, softly, to those closest to him.<break time="1000ms"/>
      We are going to build what God has asked for.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Noah's obedience was not loud.<break time="500ms"/>
      It was consistent.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Noah walked with God.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God gives guidance one step at a time.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are safe in God's care.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
